  Settlement plans against the real local stack (mobile)
    ○ skipped a saved task completion reconciles the plan entry without reopening the screen
    ○ skipped a suggested plan is a draft that reuses two tasks and proposes one; excluding changes the count; approval adds exactly one task
    ○ skipped the plan entry resumes the saved plan after a restart with current progress, never reads as "no plan" while loading, and Undo removes only the added task after confirmation
    ○ skipped a reply lost after commit is looked up and shown as saved; a failed lookup stays unresolved and never writes
    ○ skipped a retry after a relevant profile change asks for a new approval of the remaining addition, still reachable after a restart; approving adds exactly one task
    ○ skipped a lost reply to the revised review approval is looked up before anything else; a failed lookup stays unresolved and never writes again
    ○ skipped two unfinished retry reviews both stay reachable after a restart; each is approved on its own
    ○ skipped an account change hides the previous account's plan entry, cards and open plan before the next account renders
  Independent retained mobile Checklist completion
    ○ skipped Checklist completion refreshes the retained Companion plan entry
  Plan and task steps together against the real local stack (mobile)
    ○ skipped a task the approved plan added takes a step; the step never completes the task or the plan; explicit completion updates the plan and keeps the step
  Task removal against the real local stack (mobile, #367)
    ○ skipped composition: remember and edit a detail, remove and restore a plan task, retain the draft and exclude another account
    ○ skipped a removal request in a conversation only opens a review; Cancel writes nothing; the confirmed removal names the plan, reads as removed there, and its Undo restores it; the draft stays
    ○ skipped a change on another device between review and approval opens a revised review and removes nothing; the approved removal keeps steps; an Undo another device already made changes nothing
